hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2708","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Rafi', narrated to us Ibn Abi Fudayk, on the authority of Hisham ibn Sa'd, on the authority of Zayd ibn Aslam, on the authority of his father, who said:\nI heard Umar ibn al-Khattab (RA) say:\n*\Why do we still perform Ramal (fast walking) and uncover our shoulders now"","" when Allah has firmly established Islam"","" driven away disbelief and its people? Despite this"","" we do not abandon any practice that we used to perform with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).\""*\n\nCHAPTER:"""""
